The low specific activity of these preparations precludes strong conclusions concerning the function of these proteins because small amounts of contaminating proteins might contribute to activity. Thus, while we cannot conclude that these proteins are able to function in isolation, these data leave open the possibility that Pc and PH contribute directly to inhibition of SWI/SNF remodeling by PCC.
## Effects of PCC and PSC on Restriction Enzyme Access
We were interested in determining whether PcG proteins generally block access of all enzymes to chromatin or, more specifically, prevent chromatin remodeling. Considerable attention has been given to the ability of remodeling factors to increase accessibility of DNA sites, such as is measured in the restriction enzyme accessibility assay. Nucleosome movement stimulated by remodelers can also cause previously exposed sites to be come occluded, however (Jaskelioff et al., 2000). A SacI site in the 5S array template is predicted to reside between nucleosomes (see Figure 2A); consistent with this prediction, the SacI site is accessible in $40\%-60\%$ of the nucleosomal arrays in the absence of hSWI/SNF (Figure 5A). If the template is remodeled with hSWI/SNF, the accessibility of this site is dramatically reduced. The SacI site therefore allowed us to dissociate effects of PCC and PSC on chromatin remodeling from direct ef
